# Symbols of FRNG, the shooting range (the bonus stage after Brainstorm, after levels 1 and 2), decrunched at $1EA00.
# Format: ADDRESS NAME [comment], with +entry and +data lines, as analysis/main_8000.sym and analysis/puzl_17100.sym.
#
# For the RAM image with FRNG at $1EA00 only: build/ram/frng_full.bin (sha256 9470791f...5f3d91a), made by
#   python3 -I tools/ramimage.py build/extracted build/ram/frng RB1 MU1 DATAL1 SPERMA PERMA FRNG@1ea00
# (build/ram/level1_full.bin with FRNG_15 decrunched by tools/bytekiller.py, as $124A6 does after the loader, over
# $1EA00-$485D9: 170,970 bytes; in level1_full.bin those addresses hold MU1's tail and DATAL1, so these names must never
# seed a level image). $8420 also patches $1FB34 = $1880 and $1FB38 = $3FF0 (the copper list's DIWSTRT/DIWSTOP values)
# before its jsr $1EA00; the image keeps the file's words.
# Its REA/Ghidra seeds are analysis/ghidra_seeds_frng.tsv, the main code's plus these, as for PUZL:
#   python3 -I tools/ghidra_seeds.py build/extracted/boot/main_8000.bin analysis/main_8000.sym \
#       analysis/ghidra_seeds_frng.tsv analysis/frng_1ea00.sym
# FRNG's variables below take the place of the main code's names at the same addresses ($B00-$BC5: the game's
# camera, buffers and object slots otherwise, all cleared by $FE14 and again by frng_init_hw).
#
# Names: the range's logic report of 2026-10-27 (REA, Ghidra provider: the listings of FRNG's routines; bench runs of
# the original with the project's Unicorn bench and an executable model equal to it in every compared field).
# Checked with REA on 2026-10-27 (REA CLI 6.7.0, Ghidra provider, REA_GHIDRA_SEED_FILE = analysis/ghidra_seeds_frng.tsv:
# 161 functions created, 1 already present, 261 labels, 0 failed): the instructions of the 17 routines next to the
# +data ranges end on each range's first byte ($1F97E, the fade's rts, just after +data 1f972 1f97e), and no
# instruction of them lies inside a +data range. docs/AMIGA_ANALYSIS.md "The shooting range" holds the facts.
#
# FRNG's routines: reached from $8420's jsr $1EA00, from the script table $1EF88 (handler = entry + its first word;
# frng_targets calls it with jsr (0,A2,D5.w)), and from the copper interrupt (vector $6C, which frng_init_hw writes)
